Package: mufflyaccess
Title: Canonical Access, Census-Denominator, and Geography Constants (SSOT)
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Tyler", "Muffly", email = "tyler.muffly@dhha.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Single source of truth for the constants shared across the OB/GYN
    subspecialty geographic-access projects (isochrones, twostep, cliff): the
    primary drive-time access band, the total-female access denominator category
    label, the tract "reached" majority-coverage cut, the national contiguous-US
    ACS female population, the contiguous-US / non-contiguous state code lists, the
    ACS margin-of-error z multipliers, the 2-level RUCA metro/rural breakpoint, and
    the Wu-2014 age-specific pelvic-floor-disorder prevalence table (the 65+ access
    denominator). Each value carries provenance and fail-loud validation so the
    repositories cannot silently drift. Genuinely repo-specific values stay
    per-repository by design -- e.g. the cliff workforce-cliff supply/demand line
    uses a full-age Nygaard-2008 population-projection curve (a different
    cohort/source) that is intentionally NOT included here.
